===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|mi|makō|gloss=shark}}, a Southern Maori dialect form of the more standard {{m|mi|mangō|gloss=shark}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Either of two powerful [[mackerel shark]]s of the genus ''[[Isurus]]'', having a large heavy body, a sharp nose and a nearly symmetrical tail, found in southern oceans.

